#==============================================================================
# VBA-PERFORMANCE_MANAGER .gitignore
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PURPOSE
#   Keep the repository source-first, reviewable, and reproducible.
#
#   Ignore local, temporary, generated, sensitive, test-output, and release-
#   binary files while preserving the exported VBA source, demos, regression
#   tests, Python tooling, documentation, workflows, screenshots, and repository
#   configuration that define the project.
#
# REPOSITORY POLICY
#   - Exported VBA source is version-controlled.
#   - Core runtime source under src/ is authoritative.
#   - Demo and usage-example source under demo/ is version-controlled.
#   - Regression source under test/ is version-controlled.
#   - Python repository/release tooling under tools/ is version-controlled.
#   - Generated Excel workbooks/add-ins are NOT source files.
#   - Tested workbook binaries are distributed as GitHub Release assets.
#   - Local copies of generated provenance, lint, and regression-result files
#     are not source; published evidence belongs in GitHub Actions / Releases.
#   - Screenshots and repository documentation remain version-controlled.
#   - Editor state, logs, caches, build output, local secrets, Office lock files,
#     and OS metadata do not belong in Git.
#
# SAFETY RULE
#   Do not add broad rules that can hide authoritative repository content:
#
#       *.bas  *.cls  *.frm  *.frx  *.xml  *.py  *.md
#       src/   demo/  test/   tools/ .github/ images/
#
#   If a future UserForm is introduced, both .frm and .frx are source and must
#   be version-controlled together.
#==============================================================================


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MICROSOFT OFFICE TEMPORARY / LOCK / RECOVERY FILES
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Office creates owner/lock files beside an open workbook or document.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~$*

*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.backup
*.xlk
*.asd
*.wbk

# LibreOffice / OpenOffice lock files that can appear during cross-tool checks.
.~lock.*#


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED EXCEL / OFFICE BINARIES
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository tracks exported VBA source, not generated Excel packages.
# Generated/tested workbooks belong in GitHub Releases.
#
# Rules are global so a workbook accidentally saved at the repository root,
# under demo/, test/, or another folder still remains untracked.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.xls
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xlsb
*.xlt
*.xltx
*.xltm
*.xla
*.xlam
*.xll
*.xlw

# Adjacent macro-enabled Office/database binaries are not project source.
*.docm
*.dotm
*.pptm
*.potm
*.ppsm
*.accdb
*.accde
*.mdb
*.mde

# If a binary fixture genuinely becomes part of a regression contract, re-
# include it by EXPLICIT path so that the exception is visible in review.
#
# Example:
# !test/fixtures/known-good-example.xlsm


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RELEASE / BUILD STAGING
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary local staging directories. Published release assets live on GitHub,
# not in the source tree.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

release-assets/
build/
out/
output/
outputs/


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED PROVENANCE / STATIC-CHECK / REGRESSION EVIDENCE
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These files describe a specific commit/run and go stale immediately when the
# source changes. The authoritative copies are workflow or Release artifacts.
#
# tools/release_provenance.py currently produces release-manifest.json.
# tools/vba_lint.py / static-checks.yml may produce vba-lint-results.json.
# The Excel execution gate planned for v1.4.0 may emit the regression-result
# patterns below; keeping them ignored prevents local certification output from
# being mistaken for repository source.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

certification-*.json
precandidate-*.json
release-manifest.json
vba-lint-results.json
excel-regression-results.json
excel-regression-results-*.json


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REGRESSION / LOCAL TEST OUTPUT
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The regression implementation under test/ is source. Generated results are
# not.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test-output/
test-results/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL TEMPORARY WORKING DIRECTORIES
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

temp/
tmp/
.cache/


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WINDOWS FILE-SYSTEM / SHELL METADATA
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
System Volume Information/
*.stackdump

# Windows reserved-name artifact occasionally created by redirect/CLI mistakes.
nul


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MACOS / NETWORK / UNIX FILE-SYSTEM METADATA
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The runtime target is Excel for Windows, but the repository may be inspected
# from macOS, WSL, containers, NAS shares, or CI runners.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*
.Trashes
.Spotlight-V100
.fseventsd

.directory
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDITOR / IDE / AI-ASSISTANT LOCAL STATE
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The project-wide .editorconfig IS source and remains tracked. Personal editor
# workspaces and assistant/session state are local only.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
.history/

*.code-workspace
*.suo
*.user
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Notepad++ backup/session artifacts
*.nppBackup
session.xml

# Local assistant/editor state
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MERGE / PATCH / CONFLICT ARTIFACTS
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large exported VBA modules make conflict debris easy to mistake for source.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.orig
*.rej
*.patch.tmp


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOGS / CRASH DUMPS / DIAGNOSTIC DEBRIS
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
*.dmp
*.dump


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL ENVIRONMENT / SECRET / SIGNING MATERIAL
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit workstation-specific environment files or private signing keys.
# A deliberately sanitized .env.example remains trackable.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.pfx
*.p12
*.pvk
*.key


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYTHON TOOLING CACHE AND LOCAL ENVIRONMENTS
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/*.py is repository source. Interpreter/build caches and virtual
# environments are local.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

.venv/
venv/


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL LOCAL JAVASCRIPT DEPENDENCIES
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No Node runtime is required today, but repository/documentation tooling may
# use it locally in future. Package manifests remain trackable.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/


#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEEP THESE AUTHORITATIVE REPOSITORY ASSETS TRACKABLE
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These comments are deliberate guardrails for future maintenance.
#
# Production runtime source:
#   src/classes/cPerformanceManager.cls
#   src/modules/M_cPM_TIMEWASTERS.bas
#
# Future VBA source remains source:
#   src/**/*.bas
#   src/**/*.cls
#   src/**/*.frm
#   src/**/*.frx
#   src/**/*.xml
#
# Demo / usage source:
#   demo/M_DEMO_BUILDER.bas
#   demo/M_cPM_DEMO.bas
#   demo/M_cPM_USAGE_EXAMPLES.bas
#
# Regression source:
#   test/M_cPM_Test.bas
#   future headless/domain test modules under test/
#
# Repository / release tooling:
#   tools/release_provenance.py
#   tools/vba_lint.py
#   future committed tooling under tools/
#
# Documentation / governance:
#   README.md
#   CHANGELOG.md
#   RELEASING.md
#   LICENSE
#
# Repository configuration / automation:
#   .gitignore
#   .gitattributes
#   .editorconfig
#   .github/**
#
# Visual documentation:
#   images/**
#
# Do not add broad ignore rules for source extensions or source directories.
# Generated Excel binaries and run-specific evidence should be published as
# GitHub Release / Actions artifacts instead.
#==============================================================================
